 # dsFlower DP histogram updater scaffold
-
+
 This opt-in plugin is deliberately **not a DP implementation**.  It reserves a
 TreeUpdater name and a C ABI for server-authoritative privacy context.  It
 validates all required context pins, keeps the noise key out of serialized
 XGBoost configuration, and then rejects every training update.
-
+
-The v1 adapter boundary accepts only `privacy_unit=row|patient`,
+The v2 adapter boundary accepts only `privacy_unit=row|patient`,
 `adjacency=replace_one`, `unit_canonicalization=trim-utf8-v2`,
 `contribution_strategy=one-record-per-unit-v1`, and `max_rows_per_unit=1`.
 The server must materialize the DMatrix as one row per privacy unit before it
 crosses this ABI; this scaffold does not canonicalize or pool patients itself.
+The context takes shared ownership of exactly one in-memory CPU DMatrix and
+copies public float-safe feature bounds and split cuts.  It accepts only numeric
+single-output binary-logistic or squared-error tasks, with explicit public
+target bounds, base score, requested total-tree bound, and depth.  Ranking, row
+or feature weights, base margins, survival bounds, categorical data, external
+memory, and a different
+DMatrix are rejected before the updater reaches its unconditional failure.
+Gradient provenance is tagged inside `LearnerImpl`; public custom-gradient C
+APIs remain untrusted and are rejected by the updater.
+The label vector is sealed at context installation and checked again at Update,
+and an updater cannot survive a clear/set context rotation, even across
+threads, because generations are process-unique.  The context also
+requires CPU, one output, one tree per round, one exclusive updater, and
+`boost_from_average=0` when specified.  Since every Update is still rejected,
+v2 records but does not yet consume/enforce the total `max_trees`; the training
+patch must add the successful-round counter before capability activation.
+
+The required `noise_key` belongs only to the v0 scaffold mechanism.  It does
+not constrain the entropy or sampler contract of a later formal mechanism; a
+future ABI may replace it with separately reviewed sampler/mechanism pins and
+fresh entropy.
-
+
 The updater must remain unavailable to production integration until a later
 patch implements and proves all of the following before any data-dependent
 split, topology, leaf, metric, log, or model artifact can leave the trusted
 process:
-
+
 - patient-level contribution bounding;
-- public or privately selected bins;
-- cryptographically keyed, domain-separated noise;
+- public or privately selected bins (v2 validates public cuts but does not use
+  them for training yet);
+- a separately reviewed sampler and entropy source appropriate to the claimed
+  mechanism;
 - privatized gradient/hessian histograms before split selection;
 - explicit composition accounting and replay-stable release identity;
 - tests covering every egress and failure path.
-
+
 Build only for scaffold verification with `-DPLUGIN_DSFLOWER_DP=ON`.  Selecting
 `grow_dsflower_dp_hist` always fails closed in this patch.
